   "text": {
    "L1": "A fraction names equal parts of a whole.",
    "L2": "A quarter is one of four equal parts. Unequal pieces are not quarters.",
    "L3": "To make a fractional unit, cut the whole into equal parts and take one part.",
    "L4": "When the same whole has more equal parts, each part is smaller.",
    "L5": "So one fifth is smaller than one fourth, which is smaller than one third and one half.",
    "L6": "Sharing three rotis equally among four children gives each child three fourths of a roti.",
    "L7": "The numerator counts the parts shared, while the denominator names the equal parts in one whole.",
    "L8": "Now choose the fractional unit that represents one piece of four equal parts."
   },
